.TH MACHO\-DESCRIBE 1 "October 2, 2026" "MachO-explorer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
macho\-describe \- report what is in a Mach\-O file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macho\-describe
.RI [ binary | bundle ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-b | \-\-binary
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reports every slice in a Mach\-O file: its architecture, byte extent within the
file, symbol counts, and the address and size of its
.B __TEXT
section. For a universal binary this is the first thing to run, because every
other tool in this package reads a single slice and a fat header is the usual
reason a quick script reads the wrong bytes.
.PP
A slice that could not be parsed is listed rather than omitted, so that a
malformed slice is visible instead of the file appearing to have fewer slices
than it does.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binary " " \fIpath\fR
The binary to read.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write one JSON object to standard output and send prose to standard error.
Addresses are rendered as
.B "0x..."
strings rather than numbers, because a 64\-bit virtual address does not survive
a JSON number.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MACHO_BINARY
The binary to read when none is given on the command line.
.TP
.B MACHO_APP
An application bundle to read, tried after
.BR MACHO_BINARY .
.TP
.B MACHO_CONFIG
Path to a replacement
.IR config.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was read.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
The file could not be read, or is not a Mach\-O.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
macho\-describe /usr/local/go/bin/go
macho\-describe "/Applications/Some App.app"
macho\-describe \-\-json /usr/bin/ssh | jq '.slices[].arch'
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
If every slice reports no symbol table, the binary is stripped and there are no
names to search.
.BR macho\-sym (1),
.BR macho\-symlookup (1)
and
.BR macho\-findcall (1)
will then have little or nothing to work with, while
.BR macho\-findliteral (1)
still works because it reads bytes rather than names.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR macho\-sym (1),
.BR macho\-symlookup (1),
.BR macho\-findcall (1),
.BR macho\-findliteral (1),
.BR macho\-mapliteral (1),
.BR otool (1),
.BR lipo (1)